    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "REQUIRED BEFORE PRODUCTION\n1) Create PostgreSQL credential named 'Supabase Postgres' and attach it to every Postgres node.\n2) Set env vars: APOLLO_API_KEY, CLAY_CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL, CLAY_AUTH_HEADER (optional), CLAY_CALLBACK_SECRET (recommended), ZEROBOUNCE_API_KEY, N8N_PUBLIC_URL, FINAL_READY_STATUS.\n3) FINAL_READY_STATUS must match the real DB status value. Default: Scoring_for_Ready.\n4) Clay workflow must POST callback JSON to /webhook/clay-contact-callback-v2 with account_id, signal_id, attempt, max_attempts, domain, signal_type, target_titles, contacts[].\n5) Do not store API keys/passwords in this workflow JSON.\n\n### Database trigger behavior\nThis workflow is intentionally started by the n8n Schedule Trigger (polling). Every run reads accounts where status = Enrichment_Pending and joins the latest signal from signals. The upstream signal workflow writes the signal/account first; this workflow then picks it up automatically on the next polling cycle. Manual Trigger is kept only for testing."
      },
      "id": "2f041d4d-c594-4dbb-9725-c72821a11403",
      "name": "NOTE | Required n8n configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "CLAY INPUT CONTRACT\nPOST to CLAY_CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL:\n{account_id, signal_id, domain, account_name, signal_type, target_titles, callback_url, attempt, max_attempts}\n\nCLAY CALLBACK CONTRACT:\n{account_id, signal_id, domain, signal_type, target_titles, attempt, max_attempts, contacts:[{contact_id,first_name,last_name,contact_name,title,job_role,email,work_email}]}\n\nClay should honor exclude_contact_id/exclude_email on retry and return a different contact."
      },
      "id": "c554b927-48f5-4bf5-815b-8a582857f5af",
